# Every pressed layer whose absorbing buffer is sized and whose served shares are all stated, beside
# what it was asked to hold. One row per examined layer, `violates` where the shares exceed the
# slack.
#
# A share fits inside its buffer
#   The rule: a share does not exceed the slack of the buffer that absorbed it. The remainder
#   names an absorber; the absorber names a buffer; the buffer has a size. Shares attributed to
#   it have to fit inside it, which is the inequality that makes a buffer a quantity rather than
#   a label.
#
# `customer` and `unrealised` are exempt
#   They are the overflow rather than a load, and a `transition` layer is not examined at all;
#   see entries/borne.sqlc, where both are argued. Exempting `unrealised` alone is not enough:
#   where a filing states a capacity of zero, as refutation#compute does, the inequality reads a
#   clearance-side share against an interference-side bound.
#
# One unstated share leaves the layer unexamined
#   A share filed `unmeasured`, or as `sharesSum`'s output, is not in the sum, so a layer carrying
#   one sums to less than the buffer holds. A sum that fits proves nothing then, and a verdict of
#   passing would be the check supplying the missing share as zero. So the layer is left out, as
#   checks/shares_do_not_sum.sqlc and checks/exposure_unaccounted.sqlc leave theirs, and
#   arithmetic/shares_bounded.sqlc says it is suspended.
-- pm:Remainder/pm:holder against the three slack elements, keyed by pm:Remainder/pm:absorber through pm.buffer_term.
SELECT r.rule, p.filing, p.layer, p.violates, p.detail
FROM      (
    :compose(checks/roster.sqlc)
) r
LEFT JOIN (
    SELECT b.filing, b.layer,
           coalesce(b.borne > b.slack_mode + 1e-9, false) AS violates,
           format('%s attributed to the %s buffer, whose slack is %s',
                  b.borne, b.buffer, b.slack_mode) AS detail
    FROM (
        :compose(entries/borne.sqlc)
    ) b
    WHERE b.unstated = 0
) p ON true
WHERE r.slug = 'share_exceeds_slack'
